<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Magdeburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1680 CE – 1807 CE · capital Magdeburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The secularised Archbishopric of Magdeburg as a Brandenburg-Prussian duchy, rebuilt after the Thirty Years' War's worst massacre.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/archbishopric-of-magdeburg">Archbishopric of Magdeburg</a> was devastated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly">Tilly</a>'s army sacked the city in 1631. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648 promised it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> on the death of its administrator, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustus-duke-of-saxe-weissenfels">Augustus of Saxe-Weissenfels</a>; when he died in 1680, it became the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> one of its strongest fortresses and an administrative centre. The duchy was a rich grain region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg-borde">Magdeburg Börde</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenot</a> and Palatine refugees settled in the city. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-halle">University of Halle</a>, founded in 1694 in the duchy, became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietism">Pietism</a> and the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-hermann-francke">August Hermann Francke</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-thomasius">Christian Thomasius</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> lost the duchy to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-westphalia">Kingdom of Westphalia</a> in 1807. In 1815 it returned to Prussia and formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/province-of-saxony">Province of Saxony</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> as provincial capital, a role it now holds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-magdeburg.jpg" alt="Duchy of Magdeburg" width="320" height="266"><figcaption>Image: Credited as London: Wm Heinemann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brandenburg_1688_and_1320.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1680 CE – 1807 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Magdeburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick William, the Great Elector, Frederick William I, Frederick II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herzogtum Magdeburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1744&amp;focus=duchy-of-magdeburg" aria-label="Duchy of Magdeburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4942 377 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Magdeburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5262 633L5262 633M5262 633L5282 625M5262 633L5300 622M5262 633L5215 656"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5262 633h0M5282 625h0M5300 622h0M5215 656h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5262 633h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5262 633h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Magdeburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1744&amp;focus=duchy-of-magdeburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
